  <name>Sudoku</name>
  <summary>A modern Sudoku with a built-in strategy teacher</summary>
  <developer id="io.github.scott8420">
    <name>Scott Combs</name>
  </developer>

  <description>
    <p>
      A Sudoku game for GNOME that teaches as you play. Open the Strategies
      drawer and the board shows where each solving technique applies right
      now: the candidates, the cells that justify it, and what it rules out.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Four difficulty bands, rated by the techniques a puzzle needs</li>
      <li>Pencil marks, one-click candidate fill, and mistake highlighting</li>
      <li>A game clock with per-difficulty best and average times</li>
      <li>Themeable board skins and full keyboard play</li>
      <li>Print a puzzle with its solution key</li>
    </ul>
  </description>

  <launchable type="desktop-id">io.github.scott8420.Sudoku.desktop</launchable>
